  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThe southwest flow will increase across the region today with an \nupper trough digging over the Pacific Northwest. As a wave lifts\nthrough the flow on Wednesday it will bring some increased winds\nduring the day, and scattered showers and thunderstorms during the\novernight hours. Storm coverage will be highest over the northern\nzones with an SPC marginal risk for severe in the northwest. \n\nTemperatures will remain warm through the end of the week with the\ncontinues southwest flow into Montana and ridge over the northern\nplains. \n\nEarly next week as the upper ridge tilts westward and the west\ncoast trough closes off, another round of showers and\nthunderstorms will be possible across the region. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was mainly followed through this period.",
